## Why This Is Asked
Assesss ability to design scalable, privacy-preserving streaming pipelines with per-tenant controls and lineage. It also tests cross-region delivery and data-exchange mechanics.

## Key Concepts
- Tenant-scoped masking and schema versioning
- Streaming ingestion: Pub/Sub + Dataflow
- Per-tenant partitioned analytics in BigQuery
- End-to-end lineage via Data Catalog; sharing via Data Exchange
- 24h per-tenant rollback using raw logs in Cloud Storage

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo Dataflow masking (simplified)
function maskPII(event) {
  event.email = hash(event.email).slice(0,8) + "@masked";
  // mask other PII fields
  return event;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test rollout and rollback for 24h per-tenant in production?
- How would you detect and handle schema drift across tenants/regions?

## Why This Is Asked
This evaluates practical implementation of data mesh principles, governance frameworks, and lineage automation on Google Cloud Platform.

## Key Concepts
- Domain-driven data ownership with BigQuery datasets
- Data Catalog metadata management and automated lineage
- IAM-based access control with Authorized Views
- CI/CD pipeline integration for schema drift prevention
- Cross-domain governance with policy-driven permissions

